  "description": "T1 - Semi mature ash tree located in centre of rear garden- - fell to as close to ground level as possible. Reasons for the works are the tree is causing excessive shading in rear garden and showing signs of die back in the upper canopy with lots of small deadwood present in canopy. The tree is low amenity and probably self seeded from more specimen trees located in neighboring gardens. T2- 1 x mature apple tree located next to wooden cabin in rear garden- - fell to as close to ground level as possible . Reasons for works are the tree is of low amenity value as it has been previous pollarded at 12 feet above ground level. The tree is resting on cabin roof causing rubbing wounds on the tree. Ganoderma fungi bracket was noticed at base of tree and main trunk is showing signs of decay with rot pockets visible.",
